WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.448 --> 00:00:03.722
Unit three. Digital Citizenship!

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:09.945
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.995 --> 00:00:13.730
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.824
Today we learn about Digital Citizenship. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.571 --> 00:00:23.208
Digital citizen. Say it with me. Digital citizen!

6
00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:31.679
Responsibility. Say it with me. Responsibility!

7
00:00:35.171 --> 00:00:40.465
Online identity. Say it with me. Online identity!

8
00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:48.165
Fair use. Say it with me. Fair use!

9
00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:56.507
Credit the source. Say it with me. Credit the source!

10
00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:03.900
Etiquette. Say it with me. Etiquette!

11
00:01:07.326 --> 00:01:11.726
Trustworthy. Say it with me. Trustworthy!

12
00:01:15.265 --> 00:01:20.282
Community guideline. Say it with me. Community guideline!

13
00:01:23.809 --> 00:01:39.182
A digital citizen understands the responsibility of having an online identity. Following fair use means I credit the source when I use someone's work. Good etiquette and following a community guideline make me trustworthy online.

14
00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.409
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:43.157 --> 00:01:48.552
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:48.602 --> 00:01:50.188
Online identity!

17
00:01:51.226 --> 00:01:56.751
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.099
Trustworthy!

19
00:01:59.097 --> 00:02:06.732
Did you know? Giving credit to the person who made something online is polite — and many licences require it!

20
00:02:06.782 --> 00:02:09.094
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:19.004
Think and answer. What does it mean to be a responsible digital citizen?

22
00:02:19.054 --> 00:02:20.204
Great answer!

23
00:02:21.252 --> 00:02:27.599
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:27.649 --> 00:02:30.979
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

